after two months in the making and a lot  of political wrangling Israel now has a  new government the most far-right and  religiously conservative one in the  country's history despite a corruption  trial Benjamin Netanyahu returns as  prime minister thanks to a coalition of  an ultra-orthodox and nationalist block  heckling from opposition members in the  knesset didn't deter him from making his  message clear Israel's security  continues to be his top priority  we will guarantee Israel's military  advantage in the region through  unceasing empowerment the first mission  is to make sure that Iran won't  annihilate us with nuclear bombs also  high up on the agenda is the  normalization of relations with more  Arab countries under the 2020 Abraham  Accord that would sideline Palestinians  as the newly released government  guidelines highlight by saying the  Jewish people have an exclusive and  unquestionable right to all parts of the  land of Israel  netanyahu's new cabinet promises to  expand illegal settlements in the  occupied West Bank raising fears of an  escalation in tensions  [Music]  on a domestic level most controversially  Netanyahu is granting major concessions  to the far-right Coalition made up of  parties that until recently were still  on the political fringes  hundreds of anti-government protesters  gathered outside the knesset  demonstrating against some ministerial  appointments handed out including that  of etamir bengaver convicted of  incitement to racism in 2007 the now  security minister had a personalized law  passed in his name on Wednesday giving  him unprecedented Powers over the police  force other controversial laws Pass  include the dairy and smartrich laws the  first allowed Arya Dairy leader of the  Shas party to become the interior  Minister despite a recent suspended  sentence for tax fraud the latter giving  smart Rich head of the religious  designers and party a role within the  defense Ministry overseeing illegal  settlements in the occupied West Bank  critics are concerned that some of these  new policies will have far-reaching  consequences including the undermining  of the judicial system whereby the  Supreme Court could be overruled these  were all preconditions set by the  Coalition for the government to be sworn  in in the first place and we will  probably see a weekend Netanyahu because  his party is much weaker Visa V parties  like the religious Zionist because of  his a trial and because he has no  moderate party within the Coalition like  in the past this is the sixth government  in less than four years and Netanyahu  already has a lot on his plate with the  country at its most divided  Netanyahu is back as prime minister and  he says he will be the one setting the  agenda for the current government he  also says that red lines won't be  crossed and he won't be steered by what  he calls radical ideology bharti is  mostly in this position thanks to a  far-right coalition now the big question  is who will have the upper hand  Al Jazeera West Jerusalem
 

